    "fullMarkdown": "<!-- Page 1 -->\n\nSTERVION INTERNATIONAL HOLDINGS\nFinancial and Operational Performance Report\nReporting Period: Half-year ended 30 June 2026\nDocument Status: Final management report (unaudited)\nPrepared Date: 18 July 2026\nReporting Currency: AED\n## 1. Financial Performance by Business Division\nAll monetary amounts are expressed in AED thousands.\nBusiness Revenu Direct Gross\nNet Profit\nDivision e Costs Profit\nIndustrial Solutions 24,500 12,300 12,200 4,850\nDigital Services 18,750 8,250 10,500 3,620\nRenewable Energy 15,800 7,400 8,400 2,950\nGroup Total 59,050 27,950 31,100 11,420\nThe above figures represent actual financial performance for the completed half-year.\n## 2. Historical Financial Performance\nEntity: Stervion Manufacturing LLC.\nMonetary figures are expressed in AED millions.\nFinancial Indicator FY 2023 FY 2024 FY 2025\nRevenue 35.50 42.75 58.25\nNet Profit 5.20 7.35 9.80\nIntelligent Production Recovery Benefits 0.35 0.65 0.95\nAutonomous Equipment Utilization Gains 0.25 0.48 0.72\n## 3. Actual, Budget and Forecast Comparison\nEntity: Calvion Digital LLC.\n\n<!-- Page 2 -->\n\nReporting period: Q2 2026.\nAll monetary amounts are expressed in AED units.\nFinancial Measure Actual Budget Forecast\n8,500,00 9,000,00 8,750,00\nRevenue\n0 0 0\nOperating 2,450,00 2,700,00 2,550,00\nExpenses 0 0 0\n1,850,00 2,000,00 1,950,00\nNet Profit\n0 0 0\n## 4. International Financial Transactions\nReporting\nReporting Entity Financial Metric Currency Amount\nPeriod\nTrevion\nRevenue INR FY 2025 28.5 crore\nTechnologies\n2.350.750,5\nElvaris Industries Capital Expenditure EUR FY 2025\n0\nVenthor Systems Operating Profit USD Q2 2026 875,250.75\nAdaptive Resource Recovery\nOryvex Solutions AED Q2 2026 425,000\nBenefits\nNexvanta\nMaintenance Expenses INR FY 2025 65 lakh\nEngineering\n## 5. Operational and Financial Indicators\nEntity: Stervion Manufacturing LLC.\nReporting period: H1 2026.\nMonetary figures are expressed in AED units.\nReported\nIndicator\nValue\nOperating Loss (285,000)\nGross Profit Margin 28.75%\nDebt-to-Equity Ratio 1.45\nCurrent Ratio 2.25\nTotal Employees 485\n\n<!-- Page 3 -->\n\nOutstanding Customer\n1,250,000\nReceivables\n## 6. Cash Flow and Financial Requirements\nCalvion Digital LLC reported closing cash of AED 1,850,000 as at 30 June 2026, against a\nminimum operating cash requirement of AED 2,500,000, resulting in a cash shortfall of AED\n650,000.\nCustomer payments totaling AED 425,000 were received on 10 July 2026.\nThe company paid AED 185,000 for infrastructure maintenance on 25 June 2026, earlier than\noriginally budgeted.\nManagement"
